WHY ONE COMMIT FOR FOUR PLAN TASKS
They are one indivisible unit. app/page.tsx cannot compose components that do not
exist, and the components are unreachable dead code until it does. Splitting would
produce intermediate commits that build but represent no real state. Recorded as a
deliberate deviation from the per-task commit rule in workflow.md.

THE SHELL IS NOW SERVER-RENDERED
The page it replaces was a single 697-line "use client" file, so the entire landing
page shipped as a client bundle. Only the nav opts into the client now, for its scroll
shrink and mobile disclosure. Fonts come from app/layout.tsx, which already registers
Libre Caslon Text and Hanken Grotesk, so the page no longer re-declares them. The
label-caps class that lived in a <style> tag inside the page moved to globals.css as
.landing-eyebrow.

TWO FIXES MADE WHILE VERIFYING
1. The headline wrapped to four lines where the prototype uses three. Two causes: the
   prototype's text column is wider than its image column (~600px vs ~540px), and its
   display type is nearer 80px than the 92px I had. Fixed by splitting the grid
   1.15fr/1fr and lowering the clamp to clamp(2.5rem, 6.2vw, 5rem). Now breaks as
   'A home is more / than the sum of / its rooms.', matching the prototype.
2. The header carried a fixed h-20, which left the mobile panel rendered inside it no
   room to occupy. Moved the scroll shrink onto the nav row via a group/header variant
   so the header grows with its contents. Fragility, not yet a visible bug, but it
   would have become one.

THE LOGO NEEDED DARK-THEME HANDLING
public/logo.png is dark ink on transparent and disappears on the dark theme's near-black
ground. Applied dark:brightness-0 dark:invert to force it white, which is what the
prototype does with the same file (its nav mark is dark, its footer mark white).

